CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*sensor_cells)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct mfd_cell)...)
#60: FILE: drivers/platform/chrome/cros_ec_dev.c:308:
+	sensor_cells = kzalloc(sizeof(struct mfd_cell) * (sensor_num + 1),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

